      "locator": {
        "anchor": "0",
      },
      "text": "Cells are the basic building blocks of all living things. The cell theory states
that all organisms are composed of one or more cells.",
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "hash": "94e5147476abba7ebadc3cd14a6b53f703dc8442141870d6b1b615405c0331a2",
      "id": "id-3",
      "locator": {
        "anchor": "1",
      },
      "text": "Every cell has a membrane, cytoplasm, and genetic material.",
      "type": "paragraph",
    },
    {
      "hash": "9ea22173b2232c08e5f29e7d408d0ccf72e35f3a46b4113568b857b52f6c05a6",
      "html": "- Nucleus: holds the DNA
- Mitochondria: produces energy
- Ribosomes: build proteins",
      "id": "id-4",
      "locator": {
        "anchor": "2",
      },
      "text": "Nucleus: holds the DNA
Mitochondria: produces energy
Ribosomes: build proteins",
      "type": "list",
    },
    {
      "hash": "3b0fd721d34934ebd60d6f699f73e9ad3c40939b493f165f180ccfce19f7cba7",
      "html": "| Organelle | Function |
| --- | --- |
| Nucleus | Stores DNA |
| Mitochondria | Produces ATP |",
      "id": "id-5",
      "locator": {
